  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate-resilient water resources management in Somalia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;The Overall Objective of this joint co-financed Action &#xbf; analogous to the overall objective of the EU Action BREACH &#xbf; is to increase systemic resilience to climate change and food crises in Somalia.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Specific Objective (outcome) of the Multi-Donor Action is: The implementation of climate-resilient water resources management in the Juba and Shabelle river basins is improved.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This outcome contributes directly to the Specific Objective 1 of BREACH &#xbf;To improve prevention of and preparedness for food crises in communities in vulnerable situation.&#xbf;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Action has the following outputs:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Output 1: The technical and management capacities of federal member state and federal institutions to implement the regional action plans in the Juba and Shabelle basins are enhanced.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Output 2: The capacities of local stakeholders and of federal member state actors for maintaining flood protection structures and for flood early warning along the Juba and Shabelle rivers are enhanced.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Output 3: Access to innovative solutions for expanding the amount of usable water along the Juba and Shabelle rivers is improved.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Output 4: The competencies of women in the productive use of water resources in the Juba and Shabelle basins are enhanced.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
